        predict="Write the order in which the two deferred markers run and the value deferArgument returns. Then predict the closure version: does it read x when the defer statement runs or when the function returns? For the recovered panics, predict which deferred calls run, in what order, and what each helper returns.",
        pitfall="A defer inside a loop in a long-running function is the common resource leak: every deferred release waits until the outer function returns. Move the body into a helper so each iteration has its own cleanup boundary. The second mistake is recovering everywhere: catching all panics and returning a success-shaped value hides defects. Recover only at a deliberate boundary, and remember that deferred arguments are fixed at the defer statement.",
